.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \f[B]\(dqbashclient.h\(dq\f[R]

int bc_state_get_alias(bc_client_t *c, const char *name,
                       char **value);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Retrieves the expansion value of a shell alias from the bash\-server
session associated with the client connection \f[B]c\f[R].
On success, \f[B]*value\f[R] is set to a newly allocated string
containing the alias expansion text.
.PP
The function sends a \f[CR]get\f[R] request on the STATE channel
(\f[CR]CHAN_STATE\f[R], channel 2) with namespace
\f[CR]\(dqalias\(dq\f[R] and the given alias name.
The server looks up the alias in its internal alias table and returns
the expansion string.
.PP
For example, if the alias was defined as
\f[CR]alias ll=\(aqls \-la\(aq\f[R], the returned value would be
\f[CR]ls \-la\f[R] (without the surrounding quotes).
.PP
The caller is responsible for freeing the returned string by calling
\f[CR]bc_free()\f[R] when it is no longer needed.
.PP
If the alias does not exist on the server, the function returns
\f[CR]BC_ERR_SERVER\f[R] and \f[B]*value\f[R] is not modified.
