.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The returned string must be freed with \f[CR]bc_free()\f[R], not
standard \f[CR]free()\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
Alias values may contain embedded single quotes and other special
characters.
The returned value is the raw expansion text, not shell\-quoted.
.IP \(bu 2
The alias namespace is separate from variables, functions, and traps.
A variable and an alias can share the same name without conflict.
.IP \(bu 2
Aliases are a bash feature, not available in POSIX \f[CR]sh\f[R] mode.
If the server session is running in POSIX mode, alias operations still
work on the internal alias table.
.IP \(bu 2
The function uses the v2 binary protocol internally.
The STATE channel request is a JSON object with
\f[CR]\(dqop\(dq: \(dqget\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqns\(dq: \(dqalias\(dq\f[R], and \f[CR]\(dqname\(dq\f[R]
fields.
.IP \(bu 2
A single \f[CR]bc_client_t\f[R] must not be used concurrently from
multiple threads.
